stateDiagram-v2
    note left of FREE
        Two raw facts decide everything:
        a live booking? (from HTTP)
        presence (car, from MQTT sensor)
        status is derived, not stored.
        A booker may go in/out many times
        during the window (RESERVED<->OCCUPIED).
    end note

    FREE : FREE
    FREE : no live booking
    FREE : presence = free

    RESERVED : RESERVED (reserved, empty)
    RESERVED : live booking
    RESERVED : presence = free

    OCCUPIED : OCCUPIED (booked + car)
    OCCUPIED : live booking
    OCCUPIED : presence = occupied

    OVERSTAY : OVERSTAY (status=occupied, overstay=true)
    OVERSTAY : booking window ended
    OVERSTAY : presence = occupied

    note right of OVERSTAY
        "overstay" is a derived BOOLEAN, the ONLY
        violation this system has. The flap opens
        only for the booker, so a car can't be on
        an unbooked spot — a car present with no
        live booking can only be a booker who
        stayed past their endTime.
    end note

    [*] --> FREE

    FREE --> RESERVED : POST /book
    RESERVED --> FREE : POST /cancel  or  endTime passes
    RESERVED --> OCCUPIED : sensor: presence occupied (enter)
    OCCUPIED --> RESERVED : sensor: presence free (leave; flap auto-raises, may return)

    OCCUPIED --> OVERSTAY : endTime passes, car still present
    OVERSTAY --> FREE : sensor: presence free (finally leaves)
